You are developing the CHARU app (Version 4.0), a Chinese text reader with an integrated dictionary.

### General Roles
- As an Antigravity agent, you will assist the developer in writing code, handling MCPs (like Stitch MCP and Flutter MCP), and planning architecture.

### Tech Stack
- Framework: Flutter (Dart)
- Architecture: MVVM + Clean Architecture
- Database: SQLite (drift or sqflite)
- Network: dio / http
- State Management: Riverpod / Bloc
- Text Parsing: html package
- Segmentation: Jieba (via C++ FFI or Dart port)

### Structure & Architecture Requirements
- Follow strict directory structure: `lib/data`, `lib/domain`, `lib/presentation`, `lib/di`.
- Always separate UI (presentation layer) from Business Logic (domain layer) and Storage/Network (data layer).
- Use strict typing in Dart. Do not use `dynamic` unless interacting with unknown JSON structures.

### UI Principles (Liquid Glass)
- Prioritize CJK (Chinese, Japanese, Korean) text readability over stylization.
- Provide solid, opaque backgrounds for any text areas containing Chinese characters.
- Apply blur effects (Liquid Glass) ONLY to decorative and navigation elements (Bottom Nav, dialog backgrounds, app bars).
- Dark theme uses `#1A1D23` background, `#E8E8E8` text, `#FF8585` accent.
- Light theme uses `#F8F9FA` background, `#1A1A1A` text, `#FF6B6B` accent.

### Dictionary & Logic Rules
- ALL dictionary lookups must follow a strict 5-layer cascade: 
   1. Local BKRS (~250k) 
   2. Toponyms 
   3. Person Names 
   4. Online bkrs.info 
   5. Pinyin Character Fallback.
- Use Jieba for Chinese text segmentation before any rendering.
